  "description": "PEWXIC crystallizes in the tetragonal crystal system with space group I 4/m. Reported CIF formula moiety: C180 H124 Ce6 O38. From the CIF bond table, Ce1 (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Ce2 (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Ce2A (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Ce2B (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Ce2C (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Ce1H (Ce) has 9 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.765-3.815 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 116.74-117.61°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula Ce6O4(OH)4(O2CC14H9)12(OH2)6 (C180H124Ce6O38). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula). Article name explicitly identifies I(V).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
